<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's real drops 0.09 pct in thin turnover.</title>
<headline>Brazil's real drops 0.09 pct in thin turnover.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's real dropped 0.09 percent to close at 1.0800 per dollar in thin turnover in the commercial foreign exchange market due to a holiday in Sao Paulo state, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the interbank floating rate market, the real dropped 0.04 percent to end at 1.0850 per greenback.</p>
<p>In the parallel market in Rio de Janeiro, the real closed at 1.135 per dollar, traders said.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
